1	//! Generic, provider-agnostic embedding-model plugin.
2	//!
3	//! The single EMBEDDING surface — provider, model id, endpoint, and the shared
4	//! output dimensionality. The model is a FIELD, not the plugin's identity: swap
5	//! `voyage-4` → `voyage-4-lite` (or an Ollama/local embedder) by changing
6	//! `model_id`. This is the ONLY plugin that knows how to reach an embedding
7	//! provider; consumers (ctl_plane_chatbot, knowledge, memory, notebooklm)
8	//! delegate here and embed no model of their own. It is the embedding sibling of
9	//! [`super::large_language_model`].
10	//!
11	//! Embeddings are a different KIND from generation: the method surface is
12	//! `embed` (text → vector), and vectors in one shared space compare directly —
13	//! the voyage-4 trio writes one 1024-dim Qdrant collection with no re-index on
14	//! model switch.
15	//!
16	//! The plugin reports the *live* observed state. Providers differ: Ollama serves
17	//! embeddings and enumerates models (`GET {endpoint}/api/tags`), so the active
18	//! model can be resolved by lookup; Voyage is a cloud API (`POST /v1/embeddings`)
19	//! with no model-list endpoint, so it is reachable iff an API key is present and
20	//! the active model is config-driven. Either way, no active model is hardcoded.
21	
