72	/// `voyage-4-large`, `voyage-4` and `voyage-4-lite` share **one** embedding
73	/// space: vectors from any of the three are directly comparable, so all three
74	/// write to the *same* Qdrant collection at the *same* dimensionality
75	/// ([`VoyageModel::SHARED_EMBEDDING_DIMS`]). Switching models is a quality/cost
76	/// tradeoff only — it never requires re-vectorizing existing data.
77	///
78	/// `voyage-4-nano` is **deliberately excluded from this collection**, but for a
79	/// different reason than the domain models: per Voyage, "all 4 series models are
80	/// compatible with each other," so nano *is* in the same embedding space — it is
81	/// just dimensionally **capped at ≤512** (128/256/512). Our collection is pinned
82	/// at 1024, which nano cannot produce, so it can't join here. (It could join a
83	/// 256/512 collection.) Adding it to the 1024 trio would force everything down to
84	/// 512. Out for the 1024 setup — not out of the space.
85	#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, schemars::JsonSchema, PartialEq)]
86	#[serde(rename_all = "snake_case")]
